---
// VideoGrid — the nine videos of /video-center/, 3-across on desktop.
//
// Every card is 16:9 and every poster covers it, so the grid keeps one
// baseline; the video's own shape rides through to the modal as `aspect`.

import VideoTile from "./VideoTile.astro";

import { getVideos } from "../../sanity/videos";

/* ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, and it now travels with the video in Sanity rather
   than living here. Nine cards are cut from only six shoots, so three
   photographs appear twice and the grid has to hold each pair apart at three
   column counts at once: 3-up above 1000, 2-up above 650, and a single column
   below it, where DOM order IS the visual order. Positions 4 and 9 are the only
   pairing that separates at all three widths, and it goes to the tan-jacket
   pair - papa-tan-wide and papa-hero-b are two crops of one frame and the only
   pair that reads as a mistake. The storefront pair takes 1 and 8, two rows
   apart at 3-up and seven cards apart on mobile. That leaves the community pair
   at 5 and 7, diagonally adjacent at 3-up, which costs nothing: they are
   genuinely different photographs (different bow tie, tent versus sidewalk).

   The custody short sits at 5 rather than 4 so it keeps comm-n1, the community
   day with families and children.

   What changed when this moved to Sanity: dragging a video now moves its poster
   with it. In the old arrays the posters were positional and the videos were
   ordered editorially, and the two were allowed to disagree - when "About The
   Dieye Firm" was moved to the front, the videos swapped and the posters stayed
   put. That trick is gone, so a reorder is a design decision: check the pairs
   still separate at 1000px and 650px.

   Titles and runtimes: see src/sanity/videos.ts. Wistia is asked for the
   runtime once per video per build, not once per surface.

   Posters are photographs, never Wistia's stills. btxq2ysibw's still is Papa
   mid-sentence and e15abitkx1 is a whiteboard explainer whose still is a
   near-blank white frame. */
const tiles = await getVideos();
---

<section class="vg" aria-label="Videos">
  <div class="container">
    <ul class="vg__grid">
      {tiles.map((tile) => (
        <li class="vg__item">
          <VideoTile
            id={tile.id}
            title={tile.title}
            label={tile.label}
            poster={tile.poster}
            aspect={tile.aspect}
            runtime={tile.runtime}
          />
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vg {
    background: var(--white);
    padding-block: 8px 98px;
  }

  /* The blog index's ramp, unchanged: three columns, two at 1000, one at 650. */
  .vg__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: 40px;
    row-gap: 56px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* The tile owns a translateY on hover, so it needs its own box to move
     inside rather than being the grid child itself. */
  .vg__item {
    display: grid;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1439px) {
    .vg__grid {
      column-gap: 32px;
      row-gap: 48px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .vg {
      padding-block: 8px 72px;
    }

    .vg__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: 24px;
      row-gap: 40px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .vg {
      padding-block: 4px 48px;
    }

    .vg__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
